{
  "area": "discovery",
  "description": "AGSC-06-08 (amended 2026-10-02 for 1.0.0): the WHOLE discovery document, for a node that serves every route of the rule's link table and names a successor, a peer, two surfaces and a contribution endpoint. The `llms-txt` surface carries no `agsc-surface-version` and the `mcp` surface does (AGSC-11-16). The expected documents are derived by hand from the table — which links are present, which carry `digest` — with AGSC-06-08a (no `digest` and no bundle fact at Level 0, no ledger link), AGSC-11-20 (a restricted node digests only `/graph.jsonld` and `/llms.txt`, publishes no content fact and no ledger link, and names its credential page), AGSC-11-16 (one surface link per surface; `agsc-access` defaults to the built-in value), AGSC-10-12 (a peer is named by its well-known URL) and AGSC-04-15 (the bundle hash is the digest of `graph.nq`). Each digest is the SHA-256 of the file text the input gives for that route. A conforming publisher given the input emits, after JCS (AGSC-04-04), exactly these bytes; links within one relation are ordered by `href` (AGSC-06-10).",
